@using ScoreTracker.Web.Components.CommunityTools
@using ScoreTracker.Web.Components
@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@* The layout renders statically around every page (the page itself is the island). Shell
   chrome — nav, mix pill, bottom nav, More sheet — is server-rendered by App.razor
   (docs/design/static-shell.md). What stays here is the two islands: the dock slot's host
   and the recap pointer. The drawer host went with the drawers: the three pages that open
   one wrap it in their own MudLayout.

   The legacy-mix route gate is gone (docs/design/legacy-mixes.md). It was born as a crash
   guard for one page that threw on an old mix and grew into an allowlist that had to be
   maintained by field-testing, which is how it came to block the home dashboard — the one
   page carrying the record widget that works on every mix. A page that cannot answer for
   a mix now says so itself, which is a decision the page can keep correct.

   The Mud providers are NOT here. They mount ahead of the shell as their own root, and an
   island in the app bar would ask for a popover before a provider this late existed. *@
<PageDockHost @rendermode="RenderModes.Interactive"></PageDockHost>

<MudContainer>
    @Body
</MudContainer>

<RecapPointer @rendermode="RenderModes.Interactive"></RecapPointer>
<DeletionNoticeHost @rendermode="RenderModes.Interactive"></DeletionNoticeHost>
<CommunityToolsAnnouncement @rendermode="RenderModes.Interactive"></CommunityToolsAnnouncement>
